      en: "Vila Nova de Gaia, on the south bank of the Douro River opposite Porto, is world-famous for its Port wine cellars. Established as the center of the Port wine trade in the 18th and 19th centuries, it houses major shippers like Taylor's, Graham's, and Sandeman. The historic center includes the 16th-century Serra do Pilar Monastery, a UNESCO World Heritage site. The city's economy combines tourism, services, and fishing. Gaia's beaches are popular for surfing. With over 300,000 inhabitants, it is part of the Porto metropolitan area.",
